 "model_note": "SURROGATE. No faithful Hermitian-surface -> Legendre-curve map exists (genus/Kodaira mismatch), so the norm-circle fibre of PROTOCOL.md is used: for lambda=N(u0) the fibre F_lambda = {N(x0)=lambda N(x3)} on H is the union of the p+1 planes x0=zeta*x3, N(zeta)=lambda (the norm circle). Each of the (p+1)(p^3+1) lines of H (GQ(p^2,p)) meets F_lambda in exactly p+1 points (one per plane; coincident when the line meets the axis x0=x3=0). Surrogate A pushes a fibre point (zeta x3:x1:x2:x3) to the Legendre x-coordinate X=x1/x2 ; surrogate B to X=x1*x2^p/x3^(p+1). Columns = <+-1>-classes (x-coordinates) of E_lambda(F_{p^2}), E_lambda: y^2=x(x-1)(x-lambda), plus O; a point is dropped if X is not an x-coordinate of an F_{p^2}-point. Entries are UNSIGNED multiplicities (the sign of y is not determined by the surrogate). M = (lines x columns). Tautological relations = span of pencil differences S_P - S_P0, S_P = sum of rows of the p+1 lines through P (= hyperplane section T_P cap F pushed down; all such have the same class). nontaut_corank = min(#lines, #hit columns) - rank_Q(M). Columns never hit by the surrogate image are reported separately (ncols_never_hit) and are not counted as corank. rank_Q = exact rank of Gram M^T M. Protocol formula (p^3+1)(p^2+1) is the number of POINTS of H; the number of lines is (p+1)(p^3+1). The stated SRG eigenvalue list is not the spectrum of N N^T; the derived GQ(p^2,p) incidence spectrum {(p+1)(p^2+1), p^2+p, 0} is used for spectrum_residual_vs_srg, and the as-stated residual is also reported.",
